after nearly four years a wealth of  action and array of crazy costumes and  best of all and abundance of phenomenal  actors giving Suzanne Collins's novels  new life on the big screen The Hunger  Games franchise is finally coming to an  end so I wanted to look back over the  most heart in your mouth moments from  the final film Mockingjay part 2  obviously spoilers ahead if you haven't  seen the film already and if that's you  i've got a non-spoiler review right here  for you kicking off with number 5  Katniss hasn't even made it to the  Capitol to confront snow when she  already finds her life under threat  she's trying to rally district - Zoila  Stu the rebel cause let's just say  they're not exactly down with what the  Mockingjay has to say you've probably  didn't put them in the best of moods  that the rebels have just bombed them  and caused a bunch of avalanches and  just as one district - man relents after  putting a gun to Katniss's throat  another takes aim and hits his targets  thank goodness for that bulletproof  outfit hey at number four okay so even  if you haven't read the novel's just  hearing Boggs tell Katniss he's not  gonna let her die on his watch these are  feeling that he isn't long for this  world and tragically he's blown up just  after Katniss and her squads survive an  especially nasty gun trap one of the  many hellish hidden traps that make the  Capitol itself  feel like a big Hunger Games arena but  things go from bad to worse when the  next pod kicks off with what in the  movie looks like a shockingly real wave  of liquid tar or crude oil that hits the  courtyard like a tsunami forcing Katniss  and Coe to run for their lives to the  top floor of a nearby building then most  of them only just get away from that  building before snows trips arrive and  completely obliterate it  talk about tents moving on to number  three if you're not a fan of confined  spaces then Pollock's a suggestion that  Katniss and her crew go underground  quite likely sent a shiver down your  spine and oh my goodness when I saw  Pollux crawl on his stomach through that  tiny gap as they made their way through  the tunnel I swear I felt my stomach  turn over and as if the tunnels aren't  creepy and claustrophobic enough as it  is there's also a load of lizard mutants  thrown into the mix for some insanely  heart-stopping scenes which reminded me  both aliens and the British horror movie  The Descent as for the look of those  monstrous mutts that is I made me think  of the sort of beasts created by Pan's  Labyrinth director Guillermo del Toro  watching Katniss and her squad to battle  with those mutts in close quarters was  quite something  there was Gale shooting them in the head  and Finnick with his trident to name  just two  speaking of Finnick the sound of his  repeated screams for Katniss as he was  beset by those mutts was really chilling  and what about Katniss putting Finnick  out of his misery by detonating the holo  oh man and at number two in Mockingjay  part 1 you could already see that  president coin was a cool and  calculating cookie but she took that to  Anna rific extreme in part 2 when she  tricked Katniss snow and the people of  Panem into thinking that snow was the  one who dropped those exploding  parachutes and bombed the rebel medics  when it was actually her and like that  wasn't enough Coyne declared herself  interim president of Panem and we all  know how long her kind of interim would  have lasted plus she wanted to bring  back the games just symbolic Hunger  Games in lieu of barbaric executions as  she put it  vs. Katniss realized it was a case of  closer shows in Panem in other words all  they did was to swap a white-haired  dictator for a grey haired one so when  the moment came to step up and execute  Snow Katniss chose to shoot her arrow  into president coin instead freeing  Panem from coins dictatorship before it  really began and at the same time  avenging prims death and let's not  forget coins attempt to kill Katniss as  well for example by sending a still  traumatized Peter out to the Capitol  with Katniss his squad Corey thought she  was so clever didn't she and she was  arrogant the very last with her line may  your aim be as true as your heart is  pure and at number one it was Katniss  Everdeen desire to protect her sister  that saw her volunteer to take prims  place when she was picked as district 12  tribute back in the first Hunger Games  movie and ultimately it was that very  personal desire that set Katniss on the  roads become the Mockingjay a very  public symbol of rebellion against the  capital so what a terrible irony it was  that in the end  Katniss could not save both the people  of Panem and her own sister and the  whole way it played out was just  heartbreaking beginning with snows offer  of shelter to the refugees and their  children to his troops taking their kids  away from them at the gates of his  mansion to the hovercraft dropping  little parachutes like the ones sent to  tributes during the games except these  parachutes were bombs not medicine or  food - finally the rebel medics rushing  in Katniss sing prim calling out and  walking towards her only for second wave  of delayed bombs to go off killing prim  and glowing Katniss backwards turning  her into a literal girl on fire the  whole thing was truly horrifying now  what are the moments that shocked you  most in Mockingjay part 2 and what are  your favorite scenes in the movie tell  me in the comments below I've got a  special video on the way with things you  didn't know about the Hunger Games  Mockingjay and I'll add an annotation  here once it's live if you enjoyed this  video I really appreciate you liking and  sharing it and do subscribe for more  videos like this movie reviews and  things you didn't know thanks for  watching and see you next time  yippee-ki-yay movie lovers
 

